<p style="font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif !important; font-size: 14px !important;text-align: justify;color:#000;">BIS certification scheme is basically voluntary in nature. However, for a number of products compliance to Indian Standards is made compulsory by the Central Government under various considerations viz. public interest, protection of human, animal or plant health, safety of environment, prevention of unfair trade practices and national security.</p>
<p style="font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif !important; font-size: 18px !important;"><a href="https://www.bis.gov.in/index.php/apply-for-a-license/" title="Certification" style="color: #4054b2;font-size: 13px; font-weight:700; line-height: 18px;width: 100%;float: left;font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif !important;">View steps to  be followed for obtainting BIS Licence</a></p>
